To include the STOR and SITE commands in the proper locations, we need to consider the context of FTP commands. Typically, the STOR command is used to upload a file to the server after a successful connection, while the SITE command is often used to send site-specific commands to the server.

Here’s a modified sequence of client requests with STOR and SITE added:

```
USER anonymous
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,152,193
SITE <your_site_command_here>  # Add your specific SITE command here
STOR <filename>                 # Specify the filename to store
LIST
QUIT
```

Replace `<your_site_command_here>` with the appropriate site-specific command and `<filename>` with the name of the file you wish to upload. The STOR command should come after the PORT command and before the LIST command, as it is typically used to upload a file before listing the directory contents

